  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The street elevation of the building shall be constructed in London Stock bricks and red feature bricks around the doors and window openings on the corners of the building and in a band course across the front elevations in a fashion to match those used at no 7 Tolson Road and in the same configuration as at No 7 and the roof shall be finished in Redland Cambrian Solar PV Tiles or such other materials as shall first be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  The front window sills of the new building shall match those at 7 Tolson Road in size, design, texture and materials",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith (111-P-001E; Received 20 October 2011.)and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the house hereby permitted is first occupied, acoustic insulation shall be installed to ensure that the maximum externally generated noise level experienced within the dwelling shall not exceed; in living rooms: LAeq (16 hour) of 40 dB and at night LAeq (8 hour) of 35 dB; and in bedrooms an LAF max of 45 dB.",
    "Condition : 7 - The front garden shall be enclosed by a dwarf wall matching the existing front garden wall to 7 Tolson Road and shall be paved in permeable materials (such as gravel or block paving) and the permeable finish shall be permanently retained.  Any hard surfacing in the rear garden shall also be of a permeable nature or shall drain to a soakaway within the site.  The rear garden shall be enclosed by a 1.8 metre close-boarded timber fence.",
    "Condition : 8 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 9 - The development hereby permitted shall designed in accordance with the Lifetime Home standards as set out in the London Plan Accessible London Supplementary Guidance Accessible London",
    "Condition : 10 - No development shall take place until plan and elevation details of the proposed photovoltaic roof covering to generate electricity on site in accordance with the submission dated 30 November 2011 have been  submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to reduce carbon emissions from the total energy needs (heat, cooling and power) of the development by at least 13%, by the on-site generation of renewable energy. The details shall be carried out as approved and permanently retained.",
    "Condition : 11 - Prior to commencement of any work on site, details of the proposed front door shall be submitted to, and approved by the local planning authority.  The door installed shall match the details so approved.  The front windows shall be the Duraflex Tilt And Turn system in accordance with the details submitted to the local planning authority on 10 June 2011.",
    "Condition : 12 - The foundations of the building hereby approved shall be a flat slab piled raft designed by an ASUC approved specialist contractor, separated from adjacent foundations by compressible material and the foundations shall be cast immediately the formation is complete.  The new building shall be structurally separate from the adjacent houses other than by the use of stainless steel channel ties to allow for movement.",
    "Condition : 13 - Before the house is first occupied it shall be fitted with a system for harvesting of the majority of the rainwater from the roof of the house (and, if practicable, grey water) and its later re-use on site for non-potable purposes (such as toilet flushing and irrigation)."
  ],
